# Input
```html
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<button disabled>Save</button>
<button disabled="false">Save</button>
<input type="submit" disabled>
<div role="button" disabled>Save</div>
<button disabled aria-disabled="true">Save</button>

```

# Diagnostics
```
action.html:2:9 lint/nursery/noDisabledButton  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! Avoid the native disabled attribute on this button.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
  > 2 │ <button disabled>Save</button>
      │         ^^^^^^^^
    3 │ <button disabled="false">Save</button>
    4 │ <input type="submit" disabled>
  
  i The native disabled state removes the button from sequential focus navigation, suppresses activation, and changes form behavior.
  
  i aria-disabled only exposes the disabled state to assistive technology. It does not suppress pointer or keyboard activation, form submission or validation, or apply disabled styling. Implement those behaviors, including forced-colors styling.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Use aria-disabled instead.
  
    2 │ <button·aria-disabled="true">Save</button>
      │         +++++        +++++++              

```

